WPT notice

This repository holds the code, documents and recipes of WPT (Workers'
Pre-trained Transformer). It holds no training data and no weights: the
texts a model trains on live in depots.


Licenses

- Code, documents and recipes: AGPL-3.0-or-later, see LICENSE.
- Weights of a WPT model: AGPL-3.0-or-later.
- Data built by WPT's tools (corpora and vocabularies): AGPL-3.0-or-later;
  each text's content inside keeps its own license.
- Text generated by a WPT model: CC0-1.0, see OUTPUT-NOTICE.
- The packages WPT uses keep their own licenses, listed in docs/licenses.md.


Finding the notice of a given model

Each model carries its own notice, because each one learned from its own
set of texts. Look, from the closest to the farthest:

- In the model folder: NOTICE gives the licenses, every text the model
  learned from with its credit, licenses and notice (CREDITS holds the
  same list), and the output notice; README.md is the model card;
  provenance.json records exactly what produced the model, the corpus
  included.
- With only a weight file: its header names the licenses and points to the
  NOTICE of its model folder (in Python,
  safetensors.safe_open(path, "pt").metadata()).
- With wpt chat: `wpt chat <model folder> --about` prints the NOTICE.
- In the corpus the model's provenance.json names: its tables copy every
  text's credits, licenses and notice.
- In this repository, at the commit named by "repository_commit" in the
  model's provenance.json: LICENSE and OUTPUT-NOTICE are the texts that
  applied to that version.


Third-party material

Each text keeps its own license. A model can reproduce pieces of the texts
it learned from; whoever republishes such a piece must meet that text's
license, whatever this repository says.
